anita: Heads-up — we need a tiny fallback playbook snippet for the v1->v2 migration guide. Goal: one-page examples (TS + Py) showing a safe runtime fallback to v1 when v2 is unavailable. Keep each example very short and call out embedding-dim risk. Who can draft and open the PR?

kevin: I'll pick this up. Will draft both snippets + a small smoke test. Opening PR after review.

kevin: Draft TS snippet:
```ts
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new RedwoodClient();
async function generate(prompt){
  try {
    return await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-v2', input: prompt });
  } catch (err) {
    // fallback to stable v1 when v2 is not reachable
    return await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-v1', input: prompt });
  }
}
```

kevin: Draft Python snippet:
```py
from redwood import Client
client = Client()

def generate(prompt):
    try:
        return client.generate(model='redwood-v2', input=prompt)
    except Exception:
        # fallback to v1 for availability; be careful with embeddings
        return client.generate(model='redwood-v1', input=prompt)
```

sam: LGTM. Two notes: 1) call out token/latency/cost tradeoffs for using v1 as fallback, 2) if the page mentions embeddings add a clear warning about vector dim mismatch. :eyes:

docs-ci: lint looks fine but please don't catch all errors in the real example. Suggest catching only network/availability errors and rethrow auth/permission errors. Also include a tiny comment about telemetry so we don't lose observability.

julie: Can we add a single-line guidance for customers: "If you need deterministic outputs, pin to v1 until you validate v2 on your eval set". Also request: add a simple curl smoke test in the PR so we can run a quick regression on deploy. :thumbsup:

anita: Assigning @kevin as owner. PR checklist: update redirect map, add changelog note, add smoke test script under docs/smoke-tests/, include support template for possible customer queries. I'll review the PR tomorrow.

kevin: Will include a curl smoke test and small GitHub Action to run it. Draft PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4593 (will push commit soon). :shipit:

sam: Another quick flag — include this warning text near embeddings example: "Warning: embedding dimension differences may require re-encoding vectors or switching to the compatible model to avoid retrieval regressions." Keep it prominent.

kevin: Added the admonition and a one-line re-encode tip. Pushed a new commit to the PR.

docs-ci: CI run: docs lint ✅, smoke test retried once due to transient rate-limit and then passed.

zach: LGTM from PM side. Tiny wording nit: replace 'low-risk' with 'non-critical' in the prose to avoid compliance confusion.

anita: OK — merging when green. Thanks everyone. I'll monitor support channel for any incoming questions tomorrow morning. :rocket:
